          <mxGeometry x="560" y="430" width="450" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="272" value="What goes wrong:&#10;  A 'free' user spent $12 of their $15 budget.&#10;  Their Redis counter was at key rule/1.&#10;  After insertion, 'free' is now at index 2 → key rule/2.&#10;  Lyft looks up rule/2 — it does NOT exist yet in Redis.&#10;  A FRESH counter starts at $0 — the user gets a free reset mid-month!&#10;&#10;  This happened live on 2026-07-16 on charts/core-gateway." vertex="1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffcdd2;strokeColor=#c62828;fontStyle=0;fontSize=13;">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="500" width="500" height="130" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="273" value="The Rules:&#10;  ✅ APPEND only — add new plans at the END of the list&#10;  ❌ NEVER insert in the middle&#10;  ❌ NEVER delete an entry (comment out body, keep id: stub)&#10;  ❌ NEVER reorder&#10;&#10;Why not use a YAML map (keyed by name)?&#10;  Helm sorts map keys alphabetically on every render.&#10;  Inserting 'basic' would still shift 'enterprise' and 'free' — same bug, invisible." vertex="1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#e8f5e9;strokeColor=#2e7d32;fontStyle=0;fontSize=13;">
